WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.979
"The Nun" is making its way back to movie
theaters to frighten fans once again.

00:00:03.979 --> 00:00:06.720
Will the demon Valak prevail over Sister Irene
this time?

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:10.750
And how will it all connect to the broader
"Conjuring" universe?

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:16.216
On August 24, 2022, Warner Bros. announced
some updates to its slate of upcoming film releases.

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:20.510
While its most notable schedule changes concerned
tentpole superhero projects, that announcement

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:23.750
also included the first mention of a release
date for "The Nun 2."

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:28.300
The planned release date for the horror sequel
is September 8, 2023, almost exactly five

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:32.850
years after the release of the first film,
which came out on September 7, 2018.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:37.079
While less than five years will have passed
in the film's timeline, here in the real world,

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:39.970
it's been a while since a "Nun" solo feature
was released.

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:44.440
But three other Conjuring Universe films have
come out since then: "The Curse of La Llorona"

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:49.180
and "Annabelle Comes Home," both in 2019,
and 2021's "The Conjuring: The Devil Made

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:50.180
Me Do It."

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:54.880
Unsurprisingly, most of the plot details about
"The Nun 2" haven't been made public.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:58.450
But according to the studio's official description,
we know that it will take place four years

00:00:58.450 --> 00:00:59.748
after the first film.

00:00:59.748 --> 00:01:02.700
A priest has been murdered, and the evil behind
it is spreading.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:06.970
As a result, Sister Irene — our hero from
the first movie — is returning for duty.

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:10.909
After battling the evil spirit in the original
flick, she's a savvy demonologist this time

00:01:10.909 --> 00:01:13.728
around, and the only one who's seen this kind
of carnage before.

00:01:13.728 --> 00:01:15.708
"It's okay to be scared.

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:17.080
I'm scared, too."

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:20.960
The film's trailer promises that those who
watch "The Nun 2" will finally "discover the

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.400
truth behind the greatest evil in The Conjuring
Universe."

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.240
Other than that, we don't know much else about
the upcoming sequel.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:29.790
Warner Bros. seems to be keeping the plot
strictly under wraps.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:36.118
"The Nun 2" is bringing back two key actors
from the first film: Taissa Farmiga and Bonnie Aarons.

00:01:36.118 --> 00:01:40.549
Farmiga, who's perhaps most famous for starring
in multiple seasons of "American Horror Story,"

00:01:40.549 --> 00:01:42.479
plays the heroic Sister Irene.

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:46.680
As for Aarons — who's been in films including
"Mulholland Drive" and "Silver Linings Playbook"

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:51.190
— she'll be reprising the part of the titular
Nun herself, also known as the demon Valak.

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:55.090
Sister Irene won't be the only one trying
to stop Valak's reign of evil, of course.

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:59.040
Farmiga will be joined by Storm Reid as another
brave nun, hoping to defeat the demon.

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:02.759
Reid is an up-and-coming star who's been part
of a number of notable projects in recent

00:02:02.759 --> 00:02:06.500
years, including "The Invisible Man," "Euphoria,"
and "The Last of Us."

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:09.938
Reid shared her excitement for the upcoming
horror flick with Collider, saying,

00:02:09.938 --> 00:02:11.277
"The character I play is incredible.

00:02:11.277 --> 00:02:14.050
I think she really adds some funkiness to
the story and I love that.

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:17.750
It is scary, but there are so many character
arcs in the film and so many emotions and

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:21.440
journeys that the characters have to go through,
I think it works perfectly, [and is] something

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:24.420
that is going to turn into a thing that people
really love to watch."

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:28.120
Rounding out the cast is Anna Popplewell from
the "Chronicles of Narnia" series playing

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:29.120
a widowed mother.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:33.040
She'll be joined by Katelyn Rose Downey of
"The Princess" and Jonas Bloquet, who plays

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:37.110
the character Frenchie, who was possessed
by Valak at the end of the first movie.

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:39.831
James Wan has become one of the biggest names
in 21st-century horror.

00:02:39.831 --> 00:02:44.172
He's the co-creator of the original "Saw"
franchise and the "Insidious" series.

00:02:44.172 --> 00:02:47.410
He's also the driving creative force behind
"The Conjuring" universe.

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:50.599
Wan directed the first two "Conjuring" films
and produced all eight installments of the

00:02:50.599 --> 00:02:53.690
franchise up to now, receiving story credit
for many of them.

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:58.350
He continues to guide the highest-grossing
horror franchise as one of its main creative voices.

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:02.640
Wan has recently branched out in his directorial
outings with DC's "Aquaman" series and his

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.294
original horror film "Malignant."

00:03:04.294 --> 00:03:08.050
So it doesn't seem likely that he'll return
to direct another "The Conjuring" entry, but

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:11.060
that doesn't mean that he's said goodbye to
the franchise just yet.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:14.860
Wan returns as an executive producer for "The
Nun 2," proving that his influence over the

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.710
future of the series remains intact.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:19.709
After all, what is "The Conjuring" without
James Wan?

00:03:19.709 --> 00:03:23.920
"It's bittersweet for me to pass the baton
on."

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:27.420
The first "Nun" film was directed by Corin
Hardy, but the English filmmaker won't be

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:28.959
returning for the sequel.

00:03:28.959 --> 00:03:32.989
Instead, directing duties have gone to Michael
Chaves, who's well-versed with the ins and

00:03:32.989 --> 00:03:34.454
outs of "The Conjuring" universe.

00:03:34.454 --> 00:03:38.319
Before helming "The Nun 2," Chaves sat in
the director's chair for both "The Curse of

00:03:38.319 --> 00:03:41.420
La Llorona" and "The Conjuring: The Devil
Made Me Do It."

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:45.120
It's clear that producers James Wan and Peter
Safran have great faith in his ability to

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.340
bring the scares.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:50.914
In an interview with ScreenRant, Chaves spoke
highly of his working relationship with Wan, saying,

00:03:50.914 --> 00:03:52.939
"Honestly, I owe my career to James Wan.

00:03:52.939 --> 00:03:55.230
I've been a fan of his, just like a lot of
you guys.

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:58.959
To have worked with him on 'La Llorona' was
honestly one of the best and greatest thrills."

00:03:58.959 --> 00:04:02.510
The script for "The Nun 2" is coming from
the delightfully twisted mind of Akela Cooper.

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:07.319
Cooper penned two of the wildest horror films
in recent memory — Wan's absolutely bonkers

00:04:07.319 --> 00:04:09.370
"Malignant" and the blockbuster hit "M3GAN."

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:13.250
Cooper told Dread Central that she was especially
happy she was able to create a character for

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:14.959
Storm Reid to play, saying,

00:04:14.959 --> 00:04:19.651
"Bringing more Black people into 'The Conjuring'
Universe was [a] proud moment."

00:04:19.651 --> 00:04:23.590
As we mentioned, "The Nun 2" takes place four
years after the first movie, which was set

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:25.008
in 1952.

00:04:25.008 --> 00:04:28.699
So both "Nun" movies occur somewhere between
the events of "Annabelle: Creation," which

00:04:28.699 --> 00:04:32.290
partially takes place in 1943 and 1955.

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:36.360
The first "Annabelle" largely takes place
in the late 1960s, and the rest of the horror

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:39.620
franchise generally covers the 1970s and early
'80s.

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:42.920
As one of the earliest stories in this horror
universe, "The Nun" provides an interesting

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:44.920
backdrop to other installments.

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:49.120
The first "Conjuring" movie reveals that Frenchie,
eventually driven mad by Valak, later tries

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:52.020
to kill his wife, and instead tragically kills
himself.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:53.400
"Take Maurice here.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:57.259
He was a French Canadian farmer with nothing
more than a third-grade education, yet after

00:04:57.259 --> 00:05:00.410
he was possessed, he spoke some of the best
Latin I'd ever heard."

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:03.889
Given that "The Nun 2" takes place quite a
bit before "The Conjuring," it may give us

00:05:03.889 --> 00:05:06.060
more insight into his internal torment.

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:12.729
The first chapter in "The Nun" saga took place
in Romania, shooting on location in Bucharest in 2017.

00:05:12.729 --> 00:05:16.669
The horror feature also spent some time in
Transylvania, and director Corin Hardy had

00:05:16.669 --> 00:05:19.900
a priest bless the set, just in case any vampires
showed up.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:24.069
"The Nun 2" director Michael Chaves has moved
production of the sequel to France as Sister

00:05:24.069 --> 00:05:27.139
Irene, Frenchie, and the demon travel westward.

00:05:27.139 --> 00:05:31.220
Production on "The Nun 2" began in October
2022 and wrapped just before the new year,

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:33.470
with everything shot on location in France.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:37.060
Unfortunately, we're in the dark about the
exact locations where production of "The Nun

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:41.120
2" took place, and we likely won't know much
more before the film is released in the fall

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:43.039
of 2023.

00:05:43.039 --> 00:05:46.100
But from what we can tell from the trailer,
most of the film looks to take place within

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:48.090
the walls of an abbey or convent.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:52.340
While each installment of "The Conjuring"
series features the same main characters,

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:56.270
every "Annabelle" solo film has focused on
a different cast, following the cursed object

00:05:56.270 --> 00:05:57.620
rather than its owners.

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:01.300
It's possible that "The Nun" could have followed
the lead of "Annabelle," but "The Nun 2" seems

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:06.000
to pursue a more traditional sequel format,
with many cast members returning for the second film.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:09.870
At the end of "The Nun," Sister Irene used
the literal Blood of Christ to defeat and

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:13.840
depower the demon, who escaped by secretly
possessing Frenchie in the final act.

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:18.480
While this ultimately leads to future confrontations
between Valak and the Warrens, "The Nun 2"

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:20.610
addresses what Valak is up to in the interim.

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:24.310
It also follows what happens to poor Sister
Irene.

00:06:24.310 --> 00:06:28.690
The demonic Nun known as Valak is a fallen
angel who was summoned through a rift in Romania

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:30.000
during the Dark Ages.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:34.030
Recognizing the threat, Catholic knights sealed
Valak beneath Saint Cartha's monastery with

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:37.870
the Blood of Christ, keeping the demon at
bay for hundreds of years.

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:42.207
But that all changed during World War II,
when the abbey was bombed and the seal was broken.

00:06:42.207 --> 00:06:46.589
Valak kills all the nuns in the abbey, and
eventually sets its sights on Sister Irene.

00:06:46.589 --> 00:06:50.500
Though we don't know what will happen in "The
Nun 2," we know that the titular demon survives

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:55.310
through Frenchie, using him to inflict Lorraine
Warren with a vision of her husband Ed's death.

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:58.670
From there, Valak is the catalyst for the
events of the first "Conjuring" and "The Conjuring

00:06:58.670 --> 00:07:02.870
2," where it reveals itself physically, once
again taking the form of the trademark nun.

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:07.340
A demon with a similar name, spelled with
a C instead of a K, is described in a number

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:10.229
of grimoires, including "The Lesser Key of
Solomon."

00:07:10.229 --> 00:07:15.040
With the power to control all sorts of serpents,
Valac is known as a president of demons, with

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:19.479
somewhere between 30-38 legions under his
control.

00:07:19.479 --> 00:07:23.039
The main heroes of "The Conjuring" franchise,
Ed and Lorraine Warren, are demonologists

00:07:23.039 --> 00:07:24.820
employed by the Catholic Church.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:29.180
Based on two real-life paranormal investigators
whose claims have been widely criticized,

00:07:29.180 --> 00:07:32.960
Patrick Wilson and Vera Farmiga's fictitious
versions of the Warrens are considered two

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:35.537
of the greatest horror protagonists of the
big screen.

00:07:35.537 --> 00:07:36.537
"Kooks."

00:07:38.509 --> 00:07:39.509
"Wackos."

00:07:39.509 --> 00:07:43.539
"But we prefer to be known simply as Ed and
Lorraine Warren."

00:07:43.539 --> 00:07:47.440
The Warrens appeared briefly in "The Nun,"
connecting the ending to the first "Conjuring,"

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:51.159
but there's been no confirmation that they'll
return for the second installment.

00:07:51.159 --> 00:07:54.699
It's entirely possible that the film could
flash forward once more, revealing something

00:07:54.699 --> 00:07:57.510
new about Valak's appearance in "The Conjuring
2."

00:07:57.510 --> 00:08:01.039
Given that the first film reused a scene from
the first installment, the sequel could easily

00:08:01.039 --> 00:08:02.729
pull one from the second.

00:08:02.729 --> 00:08:07.419
There's also the matter of Lorraine's vision
of Ed's death, which happened in the first "Conjuring" movie.

00:08:07.419 --> 00:08:10.910
In "The Conjuring 2," it's revealed that Valak
is the demon responsible, and the creature

00:08:10.910 --> 00:08:13.290
soon haunts the Warrens and the Hodgson family.

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:17.599
It's unclear why exactly Valak has a specific
interest in Ed and Lorraine, so maybe "The

00:08:17.599 --> 00:08:21.409
Nun 2" will provide some further answers,
even if we know that Lorraine defeats the

00:08:21.409 --> 00:08:24.599
demon and saves her husband in the end.

00:08:24.599 --> 00:08:28.039
Every new chapter of "The Conjuring" reveals
some twisted truths about the world.

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:32.640
Whether they're dark family secrets, hidden
sins, or the existence of otherworldly beings,

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:34.840
each installment has us coming back for more.

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:39.150
After three "Conjuring" and "Annabelle" movies,
"The Nun," and the loosely connected "The

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:42.919
Curse of La Llorona," you might think that
"The Nun 2" wouldn't have much more to offer,

00:08:42.919 --> 00:08:45.490
but we're hopeful that it will lead to fresh
insights.

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:49.230
Previous installments, including "Annabelle:
Creation," which teased Valak's first solo

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:52.310
film, have planted seeds for the next spin-offs
or sequels.

00:08:52.310 --> 00:08:55.690
"Annabelle Comes Home" did it for "The Conjuring:
The Devil Made Me Do It."

00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:59.531
Even Tony Amendola's Father Perez from the
first "Annabelle" reappeared in "The Curse

00:08:59.531 --> 00:09:00.820
of La Llorona."

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:04.589
With that in mind, it's entirely possible
that "The Nun 2" could have a similar impact

00:09:04.589 --> 00:09:07.060
on the forthcoming "The Conjuring: Last Rites."

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:11.300
If nothing else, it's likely to give fans
more insight into the true threat of Valak,

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:14.810
and could even tease a possible return in
the future.

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:19.040
For a long time, it looked as if "The Conjuring"
franchise was rife with spin-off potential.

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:22.780
Not only did Valak the demon nun find new
life outside of "The Conjuring 2," but the

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:25.360
possessed doll Anabelle inspired three features.

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:29.770
The Crooked Man was long rumored to follow,
but unfortunately, producer James Wan confirmed

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:32.279
in 2022 that "The Crooked Man" is no longer
happening.

00:09:32.279 --> 00:09:35.690
Though we don't know why, it's certainly not
because other spin-off attempts have done

00:09:35.690 --> 00:09:40.670
poorly; 2018's "The Nun" is currently the
highest-grossing installment of the franchise.

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:43.519
So far, no future spin-offs have been announced.

00:09:43.519 --> 00:09:47.360
Only "The Conjuring: Last Rites" is confirmed
to be going forward, meaning that the cinematic

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:51.350
universe of "The Conjuring" could very well
end with its upcoming 10th installment.

00:09:51.350 --> 00:09:55.360
However, that seems unlikely given the success
of the franchise thus far.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:58.910
Whatever happens to the Warrens and their
demons next may be a mystery, but there's

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:01.040
no denying the staying power of "The Conjuring."

